In words, $C$ imposes that, in the ground state, $\mathbf{v}= \mathbf{h}$. The flag systems ensure that if $\mathbf{h}=\mathbf{x}$ and $\mathbf{v}=\mathbf{y}_i$ then, in the low energy sector, both flag spins are in state $1$.
We then choose $E$ such that it precisely cancels the energy penalty of $C$ arising due to $\mathbf{v}\neq \mathbf{h}$. This moves the configuration with $\mathbf{h}=\mathbf{x}$ and $\mathbf{v}=\mathbf{y}_i$ (and both flag spins in state $1$) to the ground state.
By an appropriate choice of couplings and scaling of the individual systems this construction works for arbitrary parameters $a_i,b_i$ (\cref{eq:sharing Ham}).
Details can be found in \cref{lem:sharing}.

