Due to the abstract implementation of all LB models against the \emph{concept of a cell} they are not only amenable to platform-transparent execution but also automatic code optimization using common subexpression elimination (CSE).
For the present HHRRLBM model, OpenLB reports a per-collision memory bandwidth of 188 bytes and a floating point complexity of 1661 FLOPs (cf. 4644 FLOPs in the unoptimized case, a \(\sim 2.8\) fold reduction).
A theoretical roofline analysis for the involved dynamics utilizing OpenLB's introspection data is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:roofline}.
