\begin{abstract} 
Given an ideal $\mathcal{I}$ on $\omega$, 
we denote by $\mathrm{SL}(\mathcal{I})$ the family of positive normalized linear functionals on $\ell_\infty$ which 
assign value $0$ to all 
%annihilate on the  
%bounded sequences supported on $\mathcal{I}$. 
characteristic sequences of sets in $\mathcal{I}$. 
%we denote by $\mathrm{SL}(\mathrm{I})$ the family of positive linear functionals such that $f(x)=\mathcal{I}\text{-}\lim x$ for all bounded $\mathcal{I}$-convergent sequences. 
We show that every element of $\mathrm{SL}(\mathcal{I})$ is a Choquet average of certain ultrafilter limit functionals. Also, we prove that the diameter of $\mathrm{SL}(\mathcal{I})$ is $2$ if and only if $\mathcal{I}$ is not maximal, and that the latter claim can be considerably strengthened if $\mathcal{I}$ is meager. Lastly, we provide several applications: for instance, recovering a result of Freedman in [Bull.~Lond.~Math.~Soc.~\textbf{13} (1981), 224--228], we show that the family of bounded sequences for which all functionals in $\mathrm{SL}(\mathcal{I})$ assign the same value coincides with the closed vector space of bounded $\mathcal{I}$-convergent sequences. 
\end{abstract}

