    where the supremum is computed as in \eqref{eq:fveeg}. Of course, $g$ is a continuous linear functional on $\ell_\infty$. We observe that $g$ is positive, indeed for every $x\ge 0$ we have $(f\vee 0)(x)\ge 0$, $f_0(x) \ge 0$, and $1-\|f\|/2\ge 0$, hence $g(x)\ge 0$.  
    In addition, for every $A \in \mathcal{I}$ we have  
