\item[\textbf{Case-IV}]   $K_n(x)$  is  $TP_2$ function in $n\in \mathcal{N}^+$ and $x \in \mathcal{R}_+$;  $f_n(x)$ is increasing in  $x \in \mathcal{R}_+$  for all $n \in \mathcal{N}^+$; and  $f_n(x)$ has at most one change of sign   positive to negative  as $n$ traverses $\mathcal{N}^+.$
