After completing the data curation process, we construct the \method{} dataset, which integrates four types of single-cell multi-omics data and spans three sub-tasks (as illustrated in Figure \ref{fig: data_stat}).
\textbf{Cell Type Annotation (CTA).} We include data from three different omics modalities:
(1) scRNA-seq Multiple Sclerosis data \cite{schirmer2019neuronal}: This dataset contains 3{,}000 gene expression profiles and 18 annotated cell types: \textit{phagocyte}, \textit{cortical layer 2–3 excitatory neuron A}, \textit{cortical layer 4 excitatory neuron}, \textit{mixed glial cell}, \textit{SV2C-expressing interneuron}, \textit{microglial cell}, \textit{cortical layer 5–6 excitatory neuron}, \textit{oligodendrocyte A}, \textit{cortical layer 2–3 excitatory neuron B}, \textit{mixed excitatory neuron}, \textit{endothelial cell}, \textit{VIP-expressing interneuron}, \textit{PVALB-expressing interneuron}, \textit{oligodendrocyte precursor cell}, \textit{pyramidal neuron}, \textit{SST-expressing interneuron}, \textit{astrocyte}, and \textit{oligodendrocyte C}.
(2) CITE-seq PBMC data \cite{mimitou2021scalable}: This dataset includes 17{,}441 genes, annotated with 7 cell types: \textit{Naive CD4+ T}, \textit{Effector CD4+ T}, \textit{Naive CD8+ T}, \textit{NK}, \textit{Effector CD8+ T}, \textit{B}, and \textit{Monocytes}.
(3) ASAP-seq PBMC data \cite{mimitou2021scalable}: This dataset also includes 17{,}441 genes and 9 cell types: \textit{DC}, \textit{Naive CD4+ T}, \textit{Effector CD4+ T}, \textit{Naive CD8+ T}, \textit{NK}, \textit{Effector CD8+ T}, \textit{B}, \textit{Monocytes}, and \textit{unknown}.
\textbf{Drug Response Prediction (DRP).} We utilize a scRNA-seq dataset \cite{aissa2021single} measuring cellular responses to the drug erlotinib. This dataset contains 18{,}380 genes and two drug responses: \textit{sensitive} and \textit{resistant}.
\textbf{Perturbation Analysis (PA).} For this task, we utilize scATAC-seq data from K562 cells \cite{adamson2016multiplexed}, encompassing 5{,}060 genes, to define two sub-tasks:
\textbf{Perturbation Significance Analysis (PSA).} A binary classification task that asks whether perturbing gene \( g^a \) significantly affects gene \( g^b \), with answer choices \textit{yes} or \textit{no}.
\textbf{Perturbation Direction Analysis (PDA).} Another binary classification task that determines the direction of change for gene \( g^b \) after perturbation of gene \( g^a \), with answer choices \textit{up} or \textit{down}.
