\]
whenever $v \in \R^n$ is fixed, where $p(a)$ converges to $1$ as $a \to 0$. Hence, one \emph{cannot} leverage any smallness in norm of $v$ in order to conclude bounds on the probability above, making it unclear how to execute the previously discussed idea with the current methods. 
