We are now ready to prove Theorem \ref{thm: MAIN} of the introduction. 

\begin{thm}\label{thm: B2}
Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $p$ be a prime number. Then there exists a bijection $$\varepsilon_n: \mathrm{Irr}_{p'}(S_n)\rightarrow \mathrm{Irr}_{p'}(N_n),$$
such that $\varepsilon_n(\chi)(1)\leq\chi(1)$, for all $\chi\in \mathrm{Irr}_{p'}(S_n).$
\end{thm}
