$\chi^\lambda\in\Omega_a\cup\Omega_{a-1}\smallsetminus\{\chi^{\lambda_0},\chi^{\lambda_1}\}$ there exists $\mu\in \mathcal{P}(ap^k)\smallsetminus\{(ap^k), (1^{ap^k})\}$ such that $[(\chi^\lambda)_{S_{ap\6k}\times S_r}, \chi^\mu\times\chi^\gamma]\neq 0$. 
Since $\chi^\mu(1)\geq ap^k-1$ by Lemma \ref{lem: Rasala1}, we have that $\chi^\lambda(1)\geq (ap^k-1)\cdot\chi^\gamma(1)$ for every $\chi^\lambda\in\Omega_a\cup\Omega_{a-1}\smallsetminus\{\chi^{\lambda_0},\chi^{\lambda_1}\}$.

We deduce that there exists an injective map $\varphi: \Omega_a\cup\Omega_{a-1}\rightarrow \overline{X(k)}\cup \overline{Y(k)}\cup \overline{Z(k)}$ such that $\varphi(\{\chi^{\lambda_0},\chi^{\lambda_1}\})\subseteq\overline{X_0(k)}$. 
