Finally, if $\chi\in\{\chi^{\lambda_0},\chi^{\lambda_1}\}$ then $\varepsilon_\gamma(\chi)=\varphi(\chi)\in \overline{X_0(k)}$ and therefore we have that $\varepsilon_\gamma(\chi)(1)=\varepsilon_r(\chi\6\gamma)(1)\leq\chi^\gamma(1)\leq \chi(1)$, as desired. 

