}:|z|\leq 1\}$ be the closed unit disk, and $p\in \mathcal{P}$ be given by $%
\left( \ref{1.2}\right) $. Then, 
\begin{align*}
& c_{1}=2t_{1}\text{,} \\
& c_{2}=2t_{1}^{2}+2\left( 1-|t_{1}|^{2}\right) t_{2}\text{,} \\
& c_{3}=2t_{1}^{3}+4\left( 1-|t_{1}|^{2}\right) t_{1}t_{2}-2\left(
1-|t_{1}|^{2}\right) \overline{t_{1}}t_{2}^{2}+2\left( 1-|t_{1}|^{2}\right)
\left( 1-|t_{2}|^{2}\right) t_{3}\text{,} \\
